            "name": "sensitivity_intro",
            "textbox_spec": "# Does the annualization method change the picture?\nDecember is a reported count. Other methods are strict means of overlapping reported snapshots, not annual death estimates. Suppression in any required period makes a smoothed measure missing. Available cohorts vary by method. Shared-within-year and fixed-all-years comparisons use identical counties; fixed cohorts may overrepresent larger counties. Filters select from those precomputed cohorts. Counts are not population-adjusted; associations are ecological, not causal."
          },
